! Responsible : Alice Biolchini
! Purpose     : Tag the version of the workflow for MuRaVes trak reconstruction and run monitoring
! Legend      : `vX.n.k` (version), X changes when major modifications are made that require re-processing of data.
!                                       *e.g.* CHANGES THAT AFFECT OUTPUTS Change algorithm, new/change clustering/tracking requirement, new/change chi2 selection, ...
!
!                                   n changes for intermediate modifications; substantial updates, but output data remain compatible with previous version.
!                                       *e.g* SUBSTANTIAL CHANGES THAT DO NOT AFFECT THE OUTPUTS, most of the releases fall here.
!
!                                   k changes for small bug fixes or documentation updates.   
!                                        *e.g.* SMALL CHANGES THAT DO NOT AFFECT THE OUTPUTS: python pakage, update of snakemake version, necessity to update container or environment.
! Date        : yyyy-mm-dd
! muraves_lib : not versioned separately. Both chains use muraves_lib from the same checkout as the
!               workflow (PYTHONPATH / editable install), so the workflow tag identifies it. The
!               version in pyproject.toml is not maintained; muraves_lib-v0.1.0 (= v1.1.0) was the
!               only package tag. A separate version will be introduced if muraves_lib is ever used
!               independently of this repository (e.g. installed in the image or in another project).
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

!================ Workflow tag v2.0.0 2026-11-27 ==================================
|Description:
| v1 data MUST be reprocessed (tag/requirements.yaml: v2): every track quantity changes.
|  - Depth correction of 2-bar clusters (method B): a cluster of two adjacent strips is fitted at
|    the depth Xc where the muon crosses the face shared by the two bars (x_pos + Xc), instead of
|    the plane centre. Clusters of size 1 or >= 3 are unchanged. Reduces the shoulders of the
|    Z/Y residuals of steep tracks (P2 residual sigma68 at |slope| 1.2-1.5: Z 5.79 -> 4.95 mm,
|    Y 5.82 -> 4.77 mm on 99 NERO good runs).
|    https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/30
|  - New branches ClusterDepth_{Z,Y}{1..4} [m]. Residue branches are taken at the cluster depth:
|    to recompute a residual offline use x = x_pos + ClusterDepth.
|  - Configuration: depth_correction (enabled, h_over_p = 1/0.97 nominal) in
|    shared/reco_parameters.json; depth_face_orientation per chain (data: Z +1, Y -1 for NERO,
|    BLU, ROSSO). See muraves_lib/configuration/README.md.
|  - Unit tests of muraves_lib.reco run in CI; pytest is in the Docker image.
|
| Known limitation: the simulation reconstruction does not apply the depth correction yet
| (https://github.com/muraves/Software/issues/32). Do not compare MC with v2 data until then.
|
| More details: https://github.com/muraves/Software/compare/v1.1.1...v2.0.0

!================ Workflow tag v1.1.0 2026-11-09 ==================================
|Description:
| v1 data do NOT need to be reprocessed (tag/requirements.yaml stays at v1): the reconstructed
| tracks are unchanged; the reconstruction output only gains two branches and a bug fix (below),
| and the golden selection also runs on files produced with v1.0.0. Same tag as muraves_lib-v0.1.0.
|  - New step: golden selection (4_GoldenSelection), writing a flat Tracks4ptree per run
|    (Track4p_run<N>.root) with the events that have a valid 3-plane AND 4-plane track.
|    https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/19
|  - Reconstruction output (3_MainRecSof): new branches BestTrack_4p_ClusterIndex_xz/xy (plane-4
|    cluster of the best 4p track); RunDuration fixed, timestamps are in ms. For files produced
|    with v1.0.0 the golden selection recovers the plane-4 cluster and recomputes RunDuration
|    from the event timestamps. https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/23
|  - Workflow output files are group-readable. https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/20
|  - Reconstruction core shared with the simulation chain moved into the package muraves_lib.reco
|    (clustering, tracking, angular coordinates, golden-track definition, configuration loader).
|    Unused parts removed (pre-reconstruction step, old per-run 1phe chain, stageout rule) and
|    step folders renumbered 1_Parser, 2_PedAna, 3_MainRecSof, 4_GoldenSelection.
|    https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/21
|  - All configuration files gathered in muraves_lib/configuration/ (shared/, data/, simulation/);
|    hardcoded parameters of the parser, pedestal reader and Snakefile now read from there;
|    unused geometry columns removed from the telescope board maps.
|    https://github.com/muraves/Software/pull/22
|
| muraves_lib-v0.1.0: first version with muraves_lib.reco and muraves_lib/configuration.
| Not backward compatible with muraves_lib-v0.0.0 (new modules, config files moved).
|
| More details: https://github.com/muraves/Software/compare/v1.0.0...v1.1.0

